[[0,1340728,0,5,0,5,"2016-10-12T00:56:54","GumbyTM","",[],"<p>The best part about this election is the death of the press. </p>\n<p>If Trump wins no one will ever trust the media again, they have burned ever ounce of credibility on the basis that they know better and the little people can't be trusted.</p>\n<p>If Hillary wins they immediately serve no purpose and actually become a risk. Expect a rash of freak accidents and suicides before their profession is regulated.</p>\n<p>So, that's a win.</p>","The silver lining in this election....","","whatever"],[1,6541862,0,1,0,1,"2016-10-12T01:04:43","watch_listed","",[],"<p>They don't become a risk if Clinton wins. They'll still be her useful idiots, parroting whatever she wants and ignoring anything that might cause embarrassment. Objectivity in political media is dead. Whatever unnatural blip of moderate, evenhanded reporting existed in the mid-20th century has evaporated, and we're right back to yellow journalism, muckraking, and personal attacks.</p>"],[2,6541957,6541862,0,0,0,"2016-10-12T01:15:57","GumbyTM","",[],"<blockquote>\n<p>They don't become a risk if Clinton wins.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>You sure? </p>\n<p>With the evil alt-righters vanquished the press will then begin trying to get Hillary to 'adjust' her positions to be more inline with what they want. This will put them at odds with Hillary who has zero tolerance for dissent at any level. </p>\n<p>From a historical standpoint a free press is never tolerated after the Dictator takes over.</p>"],[1,6541920,0,0,0,0,"2016-10-12T01:11:36","VoutGuy","",[],"<p>It wouldn't surprise me in the least if they changed side completely within days of Trump's win. Obviously people would notice the shenanigans.</p>"]]
